{
  "id": "5afa372c-0d21-4ecd-8468-da89e2cbc739",
  "page_title": "Azure OpenAI Service performance & latency",
  "page_description": "Learn about performance and latency with Azure OpenAI",
  "page_date": "02/07/2024",
  "chunk_title": "How to measure your throughput",
  "chunk_content": "How to measure your throughput We recommend measuring your overall throughput on a deployment with two measures: -\tCalls per minute: The number of API inference calls you're making per minute. This can be measured in Azure-monitor using the Azure OpenAI Requests metric and splitting by the ModelDeploymentName -\tTotal Tokens per minute: The total number of tokens being processed per minute by your deployment. This includes prompt & generated tokens. This is often further split into measuring both for a deeper understanding of deployment performance. This can be measured in Azure-Monitor using the Processed Inference tokens metric.   You can learn more about Monitoring the Azure OpenAI Service.",
